      "description": "Job Opportunities | Northwood University Careers For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Assistant Professor, Management  | Northwood University Careers page has loaded. Assistant Professor, Management  | Northwood University Careers page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Job Opportunities Menu Job Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. Northwood University Careers powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Assistant Professor, Management Print Apply ﻿ Assistant Professor, Management Location Midland, MI Job Type Full-Time Job Number 03399 Division Midland Campus Department Management Department Opening Date 09/08/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Roles Northwood University seeks a dynamic individual with strong interpersonal skills, significant industry experience and a strong record of teaching at the undergraduate level to begin teaching in the Spring 2027 semester at our Midland, Michigan campus. The candidate will be hired with the rank of assistant professor. Responsibilities Northwood University is a teaching-focused university with HLC and ACBSP accreditation offering undergraduate and graduate degrees in business-related disciplines. The teaching load for full-time undergraduate faculty is30 credit hours per academic year (Fall and Spring semesters). Candidate will be expected to teach undergraduate courses in Management, Leadership, International Business, and Entrepreneurship. Additional responsibilities and expectations may include participation in on-going curriculum planning and review; internship and/or practicum supervision; research and scholarly activities; professional/instructional development; university committee activities; recruitment and retention activities; and other related duties as assigned. Qualifications Required: Master's degree in Management, Entrepreneurship or closely related field from an accredited institution. Significant industry experience in managerial or leadership roles and entrepreneurial Experience in training and/or teaching in management and entrepreneurship disciplines. Ability to interact effectively with a wide and diverse range of students and colleagues. Well-developed oral and written communication skills in a variety of delivery formats. Preferred: Earned Doctorate or terminal degree from accredited institution (such as J.D., Ph.D., OBA; ABD candidates considered if completion date is within one year of hire). Experience teaching undergraduate courses. Expectations Northwood University stands apart in higher education with a philosophy grounded in The Northwood Idea — emphasizing freedom, free enterprise, personal responsibility, and limited government. We seek individuals who are both accomplished in their professions and inspired by the power of enterprise to improve lives. The ideal candidate will feel a strong alignment with Northwood’s mission and values, embracing a culture of academic excellence, accountability, and earned success. Applicants are encouraged to learn more about The Northwood Idea philosophy and outcomes at https://www.northwood.edu/about/ NORTHWOOD UNIVERSITY BENEFITS OVERVIEW Medical/RX (PPO or HDHP) Dental Vision Flex Spending HSA Group Life Insurance/AD&D Emeriti Retirement Healthcar