    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/northwoodu/jobs/5443447/vice-president-of-finance-and-administration": {
      "title": "Northwood University Careers",
      "description": "Job Opportunities | Northwood University Careers Opens in a new window Opens an external website Opens an external website in a new window This website utilizes technologies such as cookies to enable essential site functionality, as well as for analytics, personalization, and targeted advertising. Privacy Policy Accept Deny Non-Essential Manage Preferences Close Cookie Preferences For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Vice President of Finance and Administration | Northwood University Careers page has loaded. Vice President of Finance and Administration | Northwood University Careers page has loaded. Skip to main content Click here or press any key to continue. Job Opportunities Menu Job Opportunities Sign In Saving... Account could not be created. Please fix the errors to continue. Sign In All fields are required Create an account Username or Email Password Sign In Forgot username | Reset password Sign in with Google Sign in with Google. Opens in new tab Facebook Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. Northwood University Careers powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Vice President of Finance and Administration Print Apply ﻿ Vice President of Finance and Administration Location Midland, MI Job Type Full-Time Job Number 03497 Division Finance and Administration Department Financial Services and Central Support Opening Date 08/11/2026 Closing Date Continuous Description Benefits Roles Vice President, Finance and Administration Shape the Future of a Distinctive University America’s Free-Enterprise University Northwood University seeks an entrepreneurial, strategic, and mission-driven leader to serve as its next Vice President, Finance and Administration . Located in Midland, Michigan, Northwood is a private, nonprofit university founded on the principles of free enterprise, personal responsibility, limited government, and earned success (The Northwood Idea). Since 1959, Northwood has developed graduates who lead organizations, start businesses, strengthen communities, and advance economic opportunity. It is recognized for its fiscal management and leadership in higher education. Today, Northwood is entering an exciting new phase of growth and innovation, marked by its recently adopted 2026-2031 Strategic Plan and the near completion of its $100M comprehensive fundraising campaign. The University seeks an experienced, forward-thinking executive who can help translate strategic priorities into sustainable financial models, drive operational excellence, and ensure long-term institutional success. Reporting directly to the University President and working closely with the Executive Vice-President & COO, the Vice President of Finance & Administration serves as the University's chief financial and business officer and is an essential member of the executive leadership team. The position also serves as Treasurer to the Board of Trustees and plays a central role in aligning institutional resources with mission, strategy, and student success. The Opportunity Northwood University is at a pivotal moment. Known as America’s Free Enterprise University and dedicated to democratic capitalism and the nation’s leading educator for the $2.5 trillion automotive, mobility, and aftermarket industries. No other institution can match its unique position. The university is about to embark on its most substantial capital transformation in its history. This is not a passive role; Northwood is looking for an entrepreneurial, innovative leader to guide — not just manage — this next phase, anchored in The Northwood Idea. Leadership Portfolio The Vice President provides executive oversight for a broad portfolio that includes: Finance and Accounting Budgeting and Financial Planning Information Technology Facilities and Capital Projects Auxiliary Services Risk Management and Insurance Compliance and Legal Coordination Strategic Business Operations The successful candidate will bring both strategic vision and operational excellence, balancing innovation with sound financial stewardship. Responsibilities The next Vice President for Finance and Administration will: • Drive execution of Northwood’s growth-oriented 2026–2031 Strategic Plan. • Build innovative financial and business systems and strategies that fuel enrollment growth and long-term sustainability. • Align finance, technology, facilities, and administration around institutional priorities. • Oversee the largest capital infrastructure investment in Northwood’s history, transforming the Midland campus. • Champion an entrepreneurial culture of creativity, accountability, and results. • Partner closely with trustees, senior leaders, faculty, staff, and external stakeholders. • Steward one of higher education’s most distinctive missions and philosophies. Qualifications A record of progressively responsible executive leadership in finance, administration, business operations, or related fields is required. Experience in higher education is preferred, though leaders from nonprofit, corporate, or other mission-driven organizations with comparable complexity are encouraged to apply. A CPA credential and advanced degree is highly desirable. Expectations Desired Characteristics Northwood seeks a leader who: Embraces and champions the principles embodied in The Northwood Idea. Possesses exceptional financial and business acumen. Demonstrates integrity, transparency, and sound judgment. Thrives in entrepreneurial and mission-driven environments. Builds trust through collaboration and exceptional communication. Is energized by strategic thinking, problem solving, and continuous improvement. Provides clear, candid counsel to executive leadership. Understands how to align financial strategy with institutional outcomes and growth objectives. About Northwood University Northwood University is unlike any other institution in higher education. For more than six decades, it has advanced a philosophy that champions free enterprise, limited government, ethical leadership, entrepreneurship, and personal responsibility. The University's commitment to innovation, fiscal stewardship, and student success continues to guide its future.  Learn more about The Northwood Idea . Qualified candidates selected by the search committee will receive a detailed Leadership Profile outlining the position, strategic opportunities, institutional priorities, and desired leadership attributes. NORTHWOOD UNIVERSITY BENEFITS OVERVIEW Medical/RX (PPO or HDHP) Dental Vision Flex Spending HSA Group Life Insurance/AD&D Emeriti Retirement Healthcare LTD STD 403b/MEP Retirement Plan Roth 403b Tuition Assistance Wellness Programming Pet Insurance Discount Programs Generous Leave Plans Employer Northwood University Address 4000 Whiting Dr Midland, Michigan, 48640 Phone 989-837-4345 Website http://www.northwood.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, to the extent feasible, however, we do not warrant compliance with these\n                    standards or any other accessibility standards. We are continually enhancing our platforms to\n                    ensure greater accessibility, and we actively seek out opportunities to improve accessibility features. Ongoing Enhancements Accessibility is an ongoing effort, and we are regularly updating our technology, services, and content\n                    to address accessibility barriers. Our team is dedicated to identifying areas for improvement and\n                    making enhancements that allow all users, regardless of their abilities, to fully engage with our\n                    services. Feedback and Assistance We value feedback from our users. If you encounter any accessibility barriers while using our services\n                    or have suggestions on how we can improve, please reach out to us at accessibility@neogov.com.\n     