ng Date Continuous Description Benefits Roles The System Programmer Analyst, as part of the Systems and Programming Team, is responsible for analyzing business requirements; designing, developing, maintaining, and supporting software applications, integrations, databases, reports, and technical solutions that support University operations. This position works closely with functional departments to identify business needs and develop solutions within Northwood University's Student Information System and related enterprise applications. The System Programmer Analyst serves as a technical resource for software development, systems integration, reporting, database administration, and business process improvement efforts. The position requires independent analysis, problem-solving, and development of solutions that support operational effectiveness and institutional goals. Responsibilities Maintains, enhances, and supports existing application programs, integrations, and reports. Develops new programs, interfaces, APIs, and reporting solutions of varying complexity by utilizing established standards, procedures, and best practices. Analyzes business requirements and translates them into technical solutions. Analyzes data sources, data structures, and business processes to support operational and reporting needs. Designs, develops, tests, and maintains PostgreSQL databases, queries, stored procedures, and related database objects. Develops and maintains API integrations between Ellucian systems, institutional applications, and third-party vendors. Creates and supports web-based applications and interfaces utilizing HTML, XHTML, JavaScript, CSS, and related technologies. Participates in user consultation, systems analysis, system design, and implementation activities. Assists with the development, maintenance, and troubleshooting of Ellucian Insights reports, dashboards, and data models. Assists with the configuration and development of Ellucian Experience cards and related user engagement solutions. Utilizes AI-assisted development and productivity tools, when appropriate, to improve development efficiency, documentation, testing, troubleshooting, and business analysis. Documents application functionality, business processes, database structures, and system integrations. Identifies opportunities to improve business processes through automation, integration, and technology solutions. Recognizes areas where existing policies, procedures, or system functionality require modification or enhancement. Learn and maintain an understanding of university operations necessary to effectively support institutional systems. Collaborates with departments across campus to identify and implement technology solutions. Fulfills departmental requirements related to administrative notification during periods of illness, vacation, or professional development. Performs at or above Information Technology performance standards. Supports systems and processes that span multiple functional areas across the University. Demonstrates excellent customer service, communication, and teamwork skills. Qualifications Possess a bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Management Information Systems (MIS), Software Engineering, Information Technology, or a related field. Equivalent combinations of education and experience may be considered. Have five or more years of experience in software development, database programming, reporting, systems integration, or related technical work. Demonstrate a strong understanding of application development, system analysis, database concepts, and software engineering principles. Have experience working in Unix/Linux and relational database environments. Demonstrate advanced proficiency in SQL and relational database development. PostgreSQL experience is strongly preferred. Have experience designing, developing, testing, and supporting APIs, web services, and system integrations. Demonstrate strong knowledge of HTML, XHTML, JavaScript, CSS, and modern web development concepts. Possess the ability to perform programming, debugging, system analysis, data analysis, troubleshooting, and problem resolution. Demonstrate experience translating business requirements into effective technical solutions. Have knowledge of software development lifecycle principles, development standards, and best practices. Have experience developing and supporting operational, analytical, and business intelligence reporting solutions. Demonstrate the ability to work independently on complex technical assignments while collaborating effectively with cross-functional teams. Experience with Ellucian Colleague, Ellucian Insights, Ellucian Experience, or other higher education ERP platforms is preferred. Experience utilizing AI-assisted development and productivity tools, including Microsoft Copilot or similar technologies, is preferred. Demonstrate the ability to leverage AI technologies to improve software development, reporting, analysis, documentation, testing, troubleshooting, and operational efficiency while adhering to university security, privacy, and data governance requirements. Possess excellent written and verbal communication skills. Demonstrate strong interpersonal, customer service, organizational, and problem-solving skills. Exhibit the ability to manage multiple projects and priorities simultaneously. Demonstrate initiative, adaptability, and a commitment to continuous learning and professional development. Preferred Technical Competencies Candidates with experience in one or more of the following areas are highly desirable: PostgreSQL database administration and development RESTful API development and integration HTML, XHTML, JavaScript, and CSS development Business intelligence and reporting platforms Ellucian Insights reporting and dashboard development Ellucian Experience card development Data integration and automation technologies AI-assisted development and productivity tools (e.g., Microsoft Copilot or similar solutions) Higher education ERP systems and business processes Cloud-based Software-as-a-Service (SaaS) environments Systems integration architecture and middleware technologies Data governance, data quality, and reporting best practices Expectations Develop, test, debug, and maintain program code. Design and support API-based integrations among institutional systems. Develop and optimize PostgreSQL database solutions and reporting processes. Build and maintain web applications utilizing modern web technologies. Develop, maintain, and support operational and analytical reporting solutions. Assist with the development and support of Ellucian Insights reports and dashboards. Assist with the creation and maintenance of Ellucian Experience cards and user-facing services. Leverage AI-assisted development tools to improve coding efficiency, documentation, testing, troubleshooting, and workflow automation while complying with university data governance and security standards. Document applications, integrations, processes, and code. Troubleshoot and resolve software, reporting, and data-related issues. Assist team members with problem resolution and debugging efforts. Provide excellent customer service and professional support to end users. Demonstrate strong analytical, organizational, and problem-solving skills. Work effectively both independently and collaboratively in a team environment. Continuously expand technical and functional knowledge of enterprise systems and emerging technologies. Identify opportunities to improve operational effectiveness through automation, integration, reporting, and process improvement initiatives. Northwood University stands apart in higher education with a philosophy grounded in The Northwood Idea — emphasizing freedom, free enterprise, personal responsibility, and limited government. We seek individuals who are both accomplished in their professions and inspired by the power of enterprise to improve lives. The ideal candidate will feel a strong alignment with Northwood’s mission and values, embracing a culture of academic excellence, accountability, and earned success. Applicants are encouraged to learn more about The Northwood Idea philosophy and outcomes at https://www.northwood.edu/about/ NORTHWOOD UNIVERSITY BENEFITS OVERVIEW Medical/RX (PPO or HDHP) Dental Vision Flex Spending HSA Group Life Insurance/AD&D Emeriti Retirement Healthcare LTD STD 403b/MEP Retirement Plan Roth 403b Tuition Assistance Wellness Programming Pet Insurance Discount Programs Generous Leave Plans Employer Northwood University Address 4000 Whiting Dr Midland, Michigan, 48640 Phone 989-837-4345 Website http://www.northwood.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, to the extent feasible, however, we do not warrant compliance with these\n                    standards or any other accessibility standards. We are continually enhancing our platforms to\n                    ensure greater accessibility, and we actively seek out opportunities to improve accessibility features. Ongoing Enhancements Accessibility is an ongoing effort, and we are regularly updating our technology, services, and content\n                    to address accessibility barriers. Our team is dedicated to identifying areas for improvement and\n                    making enhancements that allow all users, regardless of their abilities, to fully engage with our\n                    services. Feedback and Assistance We value feedback from our users. If you encounter any accessibility barriers while using our services\n                    or have suggestions on how we can improve, please reach out to us at accessibility@neogov.com.\n                    We will make every effort to resolve any concerns and consider alternative options where possible. Thank you for choosing NEOGOV. We remain dedicated to improving accessibility and creating an\n                    inclusive experience for all. Northwood University Careers Job Opportunities Menu Close Menu Northwood University Careers Job Opportunities Email Job Alerts Northwood University True North Great Lakes Bay Region Midland County US Dept. of Labor Workplace Posters Help & Support Translate SOCIAL Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Cancel Clear SIGN Save We've updated our Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. Please, read and accept changes. Effective date: August 19, 2025 NEOGOV PRIVACY POLICY Contents 1. Introduction; Scope of this Policy. 2. Where We Are a Service Provider. 3. Personal Data We Collect About You and Why. 4. Cookies and