with all facets of conducting successful men’s and women’s track and field programs. Duties include but are not limited to: coaching of events during practice and competition for men’s and women’s programs, recruiting, and other duties as assigned by the Head Coach. Qualifications This individual must be knowledgeable of and in compliance with all NCAA, conference, and university rules and regulations, and must display professional integrity. Effective communication with staff and student-athletes is imperative. Expectations Northwood University on-campus facilities include: indoor 225m track and turf facility, new outdoor track and field complex (with turf football field), outdoor throwing facility, intercollegiate weight room (with 24 racks) and dedicated cross country course with 4-5 miles of trails. Position involves travel, working weekends, and working hours outside of a normal work week. Northwood University stands apart in higher education with a philosophy grounded in The Northwood Idea — emphasizing freedom, free enterprise, personal responsibility, and limited government. We seek individuals who are both accomplished in their professions and inspired by the power of enterprise to improve lives. The ideal candidate will feel a strong alignment with Northwood’s mission and values, embracing a culture of academic excellence, accountability, and earned success. Applicants are encouraged to learn more about The Northwood Idea philosophy and outcomes at https://www.northwood.edu/about/ NORTHWOOD UNIVERSITY BENEFITS OVERVIEW Medical/RX (PPO or HDHP) Dental Vision Flex Spending HSA Group Life Insurance/AD&D Emeriti Retirement Healthcare LTD STD 403b/MEP Retirement Plan Roth 403b Tuition Assistance Wellness Programming Pet Insurance Discount Programs Generous Leave Plans Employer Northwood University Address 4000 Whiting Dr Midland, Michigan, 48640 Phone 989-837-4345 Website http://www.northwood.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportuni